      ":question/id": "f297140b-f9f4-5397-9403-cc5c9d6b1ffc",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-100282",
      ":question/problem": "Find the exact solution of the equation ${e}^{t}=11.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & =11 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}({e}^{t}) & =\\operatorname{ln}(11)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nt=\\operatorname{ln}(11)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $t=\\operatorname{ln}(11).$"
    },
