      ":question/id": "06bb1232-0a8a-5e1c-9d8b-cb06e8535b98",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-100280",
      ":question/problem": "What is the value of $y$ if ${e}^{7-y}=\\sqrt[7]{10}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{7-y} & =\\sqrt[7]{10} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{7-y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt[7]{10})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\n7-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt[7]{10})\n$$\n\nNext, we write $\\sqrt[7]{10}$ as ${10}^{1/7}.$ So, we get:\n\n$$\n7-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({10}^{1/7})\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the right-hand side using power law of logarithms and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7-y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({10}^{1/7}) \\\\ 7-y & =\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10) \\\\ -y & =\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-7 \\\\ y & =7-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=7-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10).$"
    },
