      ":question/id": "d0fb4c30-2477-5421-b3da-f8a97304168e",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-100276",
      ":question/problem": "What is the value of $y$ if ${e}^{5-y}=\\sqrt[4]{7}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5-y} & =\\sqrt[4]{7} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{5-y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{7})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\n5-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{7})\n$$\n\nNext, we write $\\sqrt[4]{7}$ as ${7}^{1/4}.$ So, we get:\n\n$$\n5-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({7}^{1/4})\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the right-hand side using power law of logarithms and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({7}^{1/4}) \\\\ 5-y & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\ -y & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)-5 \\\\ y & =5-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=5-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).$"
    },
