      ":question/id": "ba9070de-c707-5661-a14c-cac1b4371745",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-263058",
      ":question/problem": "Find the **exact** solution of the equation  ${e}^{4-5y}=21.$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4-5y} & =21 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{4-5y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(21)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n4-5y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(21).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-5y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(21) \\\\ -5y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(21)-4 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(21)-4) \\\\ y & =\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(21)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(21).$"
